{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For sevenfold Cain is avenged.</b> For even Cain, who killed another — since he was humbled, vengeance was decreed upon his killer sevenfold. All the more so I, who have done you no harm all my days — if you deal with me improperly, I will take vengeance on you." "<b>Seventy-sevenfold.</b> Here Rashi explained that his wives separated from him after they fulfilled the commandment of procreation, because it was decreed to wipe out the seed of Cain after seven generations. They said: why should we bear children in vain — tomorrow the flood comes and washes everything away. But this is difficult: these words contradict those — if so, they did not separate from him because of the wiping out of the seed. Rather, one may answer: it was their assumption that the flood was coming to wipe out the seventh generation to Cain, which are the sons of this Lamech, and they did not understand what they saw in their astrology, for they erred between Lamech the son of Methushael and Lamech the son of Methuselah. And this is what Rashi explained forthwith, and this is a fortiori argument of folly — the entire language of Rashi follows their reasoning, that is: if according to Lamech's words, that HaShem is so forgiving that He does not exact punishment from the wicked and does not fulfill His word that He decreed to bring the flood upon them."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The abbreviation חז״ק is expanded here as a difficulty marker introducing an objection (וכו׳ הרי דברים אלו סותרים), following the question-answer rhythm characteristic of this commentary. The abbreviation ק״ו is resolved as קל וחומר (a fortiori argument)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:03.685230459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}